\name{cellucid_analysis_export}
\alias{cellucid_analysis_export}
\title{Export an analysis result}
\usage{
cellucid_analysis_export(viewer, analysis, all = FALSE, in_ = "panel")
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{analysis}{An analysis with a Run button. One of \code{"markers"}, \code{"differential"}, \code{"dotplot"}, \code{"signature"}, \code{"composition"}, \code{"correlation"}. Required.}
\item{all}{Marker genes only: every gene of every group (the All genes CSV) instead of the shown markers. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
\item{in_}{Either exactly \code{"panel"} (The Analysis panel); or a whole number (at least 1) (A floating analysis window, by its number (1 is the first open)). Default \code{"panel"}, the viewer's own. Sent as the parameter \code{in}.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{analysis} (The analysis exported), \code{bytes}, \code{file} (The file written).
}
\description{
Write an analysis's whole result table as a CSV file, as its expanded view's CSV button does: differential expression every gene with scanpy's columns (scores, logfoldchanges, pvals, pvals_adj, pct_nz_group, pct_nz_reference, auroc, means, cells); marker genes the shown markers of each group, or with all every gene of every group; the dot plot one row per group and gene; gene signature every cell's score per set and page (per set and group with a Group by field); composition the results per cell type with a test, else the counts; correlation each page's statistics. Refused, saying why, when there is no result or it is out of date (run it again first).
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{analysis.export} (Exports). It acts outside the viewer's state and history (a file the person receives in the browser, a publication, or what the browser keeps for later visits), which Undo does not take back: it makes no step of the history.

When an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it, the viewer asks the person first (writes-file); from R it is not asked.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_analysis_export(viewer, analysis = "markers")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
